# PPSPV7.3: ppspv7.2 plus preview-only printable-white display expansion and fixed internal H2C pre-lift feed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# V7 directional occupancy merge architecture (experimental)
#
# Planned behaviour:
# - Small directional occupancy blocks (default 3.2 mm / 8 roads)
# - Merge only along current raster direction
# - Merge neighbouring blocks only if enough same-line continuity exists
# - Default continuity threshold:
#       join_gap_mm <= 0.10 mm
#       >= 3 touching lines out of 8
# - Endpoint trim compensation applied LAST after topology decisions
#
# NOTE:
# Current file exposes the parameters and architecture hooks.
# Full merge planner implementation still to be completed/tested.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#!/usr/bin/env python3
# v1.100: fixes profile endpoint-trim override so explicit start/end trim replaces, rather than adds to, global endpoint trim.
"""
fc3d_v5_picture_compiler_lut_spanhop_candidate_040native_geom3mf_master_studioraster.py

V5 F-stack image-to-.gcode.3mf compiler foundation with aggressive Studio-like raster mode.

Key ideas:
- W opaque white base, F translucent eSUN white, S static translucent separator, R/G/B/C/Y absorbers
- 0.2 mm W base + 8 x 0.1 mm mixing layers
- 0.40 mm image-native colour pixels, 0.40 mm roads
- 1 source image pixel = 1 printed 0.40 mm colour cell; no hidden subpixel averaging
- no halftones, no line sorting
- Colour sorting is currently disabled for optical-stack experiments; optimiser code is retained but not called
- Optional recipe lookup/codebook mode maps each 0.40 mm image pixel/cell to nearest predicted recipe in RGB space; preview-only mode can output the predicted printed appearance without generating G-code
- 2026-06-30 layer-order convention: layer_01 / stack slot 0 is the lowest optical layer; recipes and direct-layer image lists are bottom-to-top.
- default recipe generator does NOT yet emit S
- direct deterministic roads, solid prime tower, full Bambu/H2C toolchange blocks from template
- selective Z-hop uses a per-layer exact span index, not a raster height field
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse, base64, csv, hashlib, json, math, os, re, zipfile, io, time
from dataclasses import dataclass
import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET

