# v1.156: hardens prime-tower geometry and H2C M620.14 staging without changing model/card emission.
# Secondary interleaved tower roads are emitted as isolated horizontal strokes so they cannot
# retrace primary edge connectors or cross previously printed same-layer tower centrelines.
# M620.14 defaults to a reserved staging point 2.0 mm outside the tower entry edge instead of
# inside the printed tower.  New fail-closed audits reject any positive-length same-layer tower
# centreline reprint/proper crossing and reject non-template M620.14 staging that enters the
# tower, leaves the printable area, or violates the reserved clearance.
#
# v1.155: makes 0.40-mm logical ownership the universal same-layer infill rule.
# Every logical 0.40-mm pixel/road wholly owns the offset filter/infill sampled
# from that pixel.  The physical +0.20-mm phase may place that extrusion in a
# valley between different neighbouring carrier materials/owners; that geometric
# overlap never creates shared, half-road or transition ownership.  Validation
# now checks the source pixel's own owner/carrier contract and logical cross-layer
# owner consistency.  Neighbour-carrier differences are diagnostic only, never
# an ownership error.  No print geometry, phase, VE, pressure, endpoint trim or
# scheduler mechanics are changed from v1.154.
#
# v1.152: preserves the calibrated S250_TILT20 under-recovery without logical prime-state drift.
# A physical calibrated full reprime (currently +0.395 mm) is an explicit logical transition
# 0.00 -> FULL_PRIME_STATE (0.400), while the physical end retract remains the full 0.400 mm.
# Pressure values are named constants below so the empirical bias can be retuned without changing
# state-machine logic. Retraction remains permissive/clipped; priming remains strict/state-checked.
#
# v1.151: adds one authoritative numeric prime-state machine over the complete FC3D model-motion body.
# prime_state=0.00 fully retracted, 0.38 pre-primed, 0.40 fully primed; arbitrary intermediate
# states are tracked exactly. Retractions are permissive and clipped so state never drops below zero;
# prime/recovery operations are state-validated and may never exceed 0.40. Any dry XYZ move while live
# is automatically preceded by the exact outstanding retract, and a formerly pressure-chained next road
# receives a canonical +0.38/+0.02 reprime. H2C filament-swap unload relief is explicitly outside this
# print-pressure state because it is filament handling, not nozzle pressure bookkeeping.
#
# v1.150: fixes active-layer prime-tower pressure isolation: prewipe remains retracted through all
# non-extruding repositioning and reprimes only at the next extrusion start; toolchange tower
# exits retract the full 0.40 mm immediately at print stop before any Z/XY travel. Adds explicit
# tower pressure-state audit markers. Base-raster pressure behaviour is intentionally unchanged.
#
# v1.149: extends card-encoded atomic same-layer partition ownership with cross-layer
# support-footprint ownership and endpoint-proximity audits. Normal carrier
# and paired infill runs are both hard-split at the same partition boundaries,
# even when material and dose are identical on both sides. A fail-closed source
# audit also rejects active infill in mixed partition/material/dose valleys.
# v1.147: makes direct G29.1 trim change detection use the same exact five-
# decimal precision that is emitted to G-code. A mathematically distinct trim
# that formats to the inherited baseline (for example -0.019999075 -> -0.02000)
# is now treated as unchanged, so no redundant trim-begin/set/restore block is
# emitted. The variable-height audit uses the same quantised comparison. This
# changes no physically representable G29.1 command, TILT20 depth law, VE,
# pressure cycle, raster geometry, endpoint trim, toolchange, or layer logic.
#
# v1.146: re-activates logical F as a first-class clear/transparent carrier
# for direct-layer FC3D experiments. F is structurally a normal carrier, not a
# chromatic Z-offset material. Job material discovery/tower/audits now permit
# W,F,R,Y,G,C,B. Runtime H2C production slots are updated to the requested
# one-based F=7 and R=8 (raw F=6, R=7), with every logical material retaining a
# distinct filament slot. F, R, Y, G, C and B remain assigned to the physical
# right hotend; W remains on the left. Direct diagnostic preview treats F as
# optically neutral/clear rather than displaying its internal orange identity
# colour. No filter/TILT20, endpoint, raster, old-VE-height, or G29 mechanics
# are changed.
#
# v1.145: corrects the meaning of "old VE" when deliberately reused for a
# high-VE normal carrier. Historical pre-4x4/direct-infill VE changed E only
# at the ordinary nominal layer plane; carrier-height scaling was introduced
# later for the 4x4 carrier/filter experiment. Add card-selectable
