# v1.141: clean floating-point direct-image dose path, rebuilt directly from
# v1.139. The abandoned v1.140 side-channel metadata dose-grid experiment is
# NOT inherited.
#
# Float TIFF direct sheets use normalized float32 RGBA:
#     RGB = material debug colour in 0..1
#     A   = exact extrusion dose fraction in 0..1
#
# Therefore A=0.005 means exactly 0.5% VE, A=0.010 means exactly 1.0% VE,
# ... A=1.000 means 100% VE. The same exact floating dose reaches both E
# scaling and the existing continuous TILT20 VE->physical-height function.
#
# Legacy PNG/RGBA cards remain unchanged:
#     alpha 128 = 100% VE
#     dose = alpha/128
#
# v1.139: scheduler emission-contract correction only.
# v1.138 correctly restored carrier-height metadata inside the precompiled
# normal carrier segments, but the scheduler emission unit still advertised
# carrier_height_grid=None for normal actions. The downstream emitter therefore
# failed to enter the proven direct/reference-wipe path even though each segment
# carried height_fraction=1.0.
#
# Normal scheduler actions now advertise DIRECT_CARRIER_HEIGHT_GRID. Because
# precompiled carrier segments are already audited dose=1.0, height=1.0 and
# profile=-1, this does not alter carrier geometry or height; it only restores
# the successful v6.35 per-road pressure transition contract.
# v1.138: two narrowly-scoped corrections found by executable comparison
# against the physically flawless v6.35 / v1.125 S250 Row-6 reference.
#
# (1) SAME-LAYER FILTER PHYSICAL-Z REPRESENTATION
#     The TILT20 depth law was calibrated while B was represented at the next
#     nominal plane (old logical/physical layer 2, nominal Z0.400). Reassigning
#     that same optical operation to logical layer 1 must NOT lower the physical
#     nozzle by another 0.100 mm. For operation=filter_zoffset only, keep model
#     G1 Z at the current layer nominal Z but translate absolute G29.1 upward by
#     exactly MIX_H_MM. Therefore:
#
#         new same-layer effective Z
#           = Z_current + (baseline - depth + MIX_H_MM)
#           = Z_next    + (baseline - depth)
#
#     This is a representation correction, not a change to the TILT20 curve.
#
# (2) CARRIER PRESSURE CONTRACT
#     v1.137 correctly removed FILTER profile IDs from normal carrier topology,
#     but also removed the carrier-height field and accidentally disabled the
#     proven per-road reference-wipe pressure path. Restore the normal carrier's
#     own height grid while continuing to exclude filter profile metadata.
#     Complete-carrier mode proves dose=1 and height_fraction=1, so only an
#     actual carrier MATERIAL change can split a carrier road.
# v1.137: same-layer carrier continuity fix. In all_or_defer mode the normal
# carrier compiler must be completely independent of paired/filter Z-offset
# metadata. Normal carrier roads are therefore compiled WITHOUT the filter
# carrier-height grid and WITHOUT the filter height-profile grid. With the
# complete-carrier contract already enforcing 100% carrier dose, a carrier road
# may now split only when its carrier MATERIAL changes along that scanline.
# Filter/infill compilation is unchanged and still receives its independent
# dose, G29.1 height-profile and half-road valley-phase metadata.
# v1.136: clean reconstruction for repeating-layer validation. Preserve the
# physically reconfirmed v1.125 path planner exactly (virtual XY=(0,0), stable
# axis-local bins, broad-panel edge entry) and retain its v1.124 tower-exit
# pressure-isolation behaviour. Carry forward the integrated same-layer
# architecture/fixes through corrected v1.134: same-Z filter-Zoffset support,
# runtime-active tower audit, complete-carrier bounded-valley all_or_defer
# scheduling, complete primary/secondary tower filling, physical-index-owned
# layer boundaries, primary structural-fill tower audit marker, and canonical
# 0=X/odd=Y/even=X raster parity. Abandoned v1.135 is excluded.
# v1.134: restore the correct raster parity after accounting for logical/base
# layer 0. Layer 0 is X/left-right, therefore odd optical/logical layers
# (1,3,5,7,...) are Y/front-back and even layers (2,4,6,8,...) are
# X/left-right. Same-layer paired infill remains hard-wired to the exact same
# orientation as its carrier. Retains v1.133's missing primary tower-slot audit
# marker fix. No Z/VE/endpoint/pressure/toolchange/scheduler-order/layer-boundary
# mechanics changed.
# v1.131: make emission_unit["physical"] the sole authority for physical-layer boundaries.
# CHANGE_LAYER is emitted only when that index advances. The existing per-action
# new_physical_layer declaration is retained only as a fail-closed consistency
